			"type": "text",
			"text": "Tethybatis selachoides is a species of thornback ray known discovered near Nardò in Italy. Its name means 'Tethyan ray having the form of a shark', referring to its location within the Tethys Sea and its resemblance of its tail, dorsal, and caudal fins to those of a shark. The animal was preserved with skin, showing it didn't have the spines typical of modern thornback rays."
